.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-dispute - Open a dispute (payer-submitted, signal-only): prepare, sign, broadcast


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments dispute  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepare the transaction that calls dispute() on the RAIL0 contract, then
sign and submit it like any other operation (the gateway broadcasts it).

.PP
Disputes are payer-driven and signal-only: they move no money. Only the payer
may dispute, while the refund window is open and the merchant holds the funds.

.PP
A reason is required: --reason takes a code from the gateway's dispute-reason
dictionary (e.g. not_received, duplicate, other) or exactly its bytes32. It is
checked locally before anything is sent; on a terminal, leaving it out offers
the list. 'rail0 disputes reasons' lists the codes and what they mean.

.PP
Signal-only does not mean instant: it is still an on-chain transaction, so the
API returns 202 and the dispute is not visible until it confirms. Add -w/--wait
to block until it does (or fails).

.PP
Pass --private-key (-p): the CLI signs locally with the payer key and broadcasts.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for dispute

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	Make a re-run safe: the same key returns the first transaction instead of opening a second

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Caller's secp256k1 private key (0x-prefixed hex); signs and broadcasts in one step

.PP
\fB--reason\fP=""
	Required. Why the dispute is opened: a code from 'rail0 disputes reasons' (open list) or its bytes32

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=15m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set; unset, 10× the chain's measured p90 settlement, kept within 5m–15m

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments dispute 0xrail0Id… -p @buyer-key --reason not_received --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP, \fBrail0-payments-dispute-close(1)\fP
